      "answer": "The customer whose issue started after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout is BlueHarbor Logistics. Their search relevance degraded due to the taxonomy change rolled out on 2026-02-20, causing saved searches to return low-relevance hits and duplicates, increasing manual triage time significantly.\n\nTo get BlueHarbor comfortable with renewal, we proposed a short-term proof plan involving updating index weighting and adding a translation/mapping layer to map new taxonomy terms to historical query tokens for the top 20 saved searches. This includes an A/B test in staging lasting 7-10 business days to tune and validate, with acceptance criteria such as achieving a top-5 correct hit rate of at least 80% for prioritized queries, no regression in EN-RULES-ENGINE suppression logic, and incident correlation latency under 200ms. A 90-day professional services engagement at a fixed price of $48k was offered to implement this, with a 30% discount if BlueHarbor signs an Orchestrator expansion concurrently. Additionally, a conditional credit on renewal was proposed if the proof does not meet the agreed accuracy uplift within 10 business days [art_bd3560dfe194, art_0bccc580184e]. \n\nNo other customers with issues starting after the 2026-02-20 taxonomy rollout and their proof plans were identified in the evidence.",
