      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were the \"department\" and \"businessUnit\" attributes, which were used inconsistently across teams\u2014Merchant Services used businessUnit=merchant, while Payments Ops used department=payments. This inconsistency caused ingestion normalization failures and routing mismatches in the Rules Engine. Jin proposed a fast fix to add a preprocessing mapping rule in Signal Ingest to normalize these fields by mapping businessUnit to department (or vice versa) and publishing a canonical normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a configuration-only change, hot-reloadable, and does not require any Okta flow changes or appliance restarts, thus avoiding waiting on Okta change control [art_79f625aafa16][art_e60697c15fce].",
